 "title": "Gene Expression and Antioxidant Research in Dendrobium officinale",
 "summary": "This cluster is centered around the plant Dendrobium officinale, which is the subject of various research studies. The gene DoUGT71K2 is expressed in D. officinale and is activated by the gene DoMYB102. The DESeq2 method was used to analyze gene expression in D. officinale using the WRS method. The Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute published research on D. officinale in the Vet Sci journal, which was authored by Jeon Hyuncheol, Kim Haham, and Lee Seunghyung. The RNA method was used by C.J. Siddique to study D. officinale. The plant is also associated with antioxidants, which may be related to the presence of the UDP-glycosyltransferases gene. The research on D. officinale was conducted at Pukyong National University, where Jeon Hyuncheol, Kim Haham, and Lee Seunghyung are affiliated.",
